    <description>Mail cycle of one campaign member (generic, any campaign with Max Attempts (Mail)): Waiting -&gt; Due (mail 1) once the batch is released, the next mail on the days of the Mail Schedule (Days), in business days (Sales (NL), Util_BusinessDays) counted from the release (empty: every Mail Interval (Days)) while there is no answer, Completed on the last schedule day after the last mail (+ Mail Completed Status; in a staged campaign the member then moves from Operational to the Not reacted campaign, Svc_CampaignMove), Stopped as soon as Response is filled. Growth sends the mail that is Due. Called daily by stf - CampaignMember - Mail Cycle.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Business days after the release for the next step (Mail Schedule (Days) value); 0 when there is none.</description>
        <name>fScheduleDays</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!fScheduleDayText}), 0, VALUE({!fScheduleDayText}))</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>fLastMail</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>BLANKVALUE({!rCampaignMember.MailNumber__c}, 0) &gt;= BLANKVALUE({!rCampaign.MaxMailAttempts__c}, 1)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>fNextMailNumber</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>BLANKVALUE({!rCampaignMember.MailNumber__c}, 0) + 1</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>fNextMailReached</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!rCampaignMember.MailDueOn__c}), TRUE,
IF(OR(ISBLANK({!fScheduleDayText}), ISBLANK({!rCampaignMember.MailBatchReleasedOn__c})),
{!rCampaignMember.MailDueOn__c} + BLANKVALUE({!rCampaign.MailIntervalDays__c}, 14) &lt;= {!$Flow.CurrentDate},
{!vScheduleDue} &lt;= {!$Flow.CurrentDate}))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Day (after mail 1) of the step after the current mail, from the campaign Mail Schedule (Days), e.g. "3,8,14" (business days): mail 1 → 3, mail 2 → 8, mail 3 → 14 (closing day). Blank when there is no schedule or no value for this mail.</description>
        <name>fScheduleDayText</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>TRIM(MID(SUBSTITUTE(SUBSTITUTE({!rCampaign.MailScheduleDays__c}, &apos; &apos;, &apos;&apos;), &apos;,&apos;, &apos;                    &apos;), (BLANKVALUE({!rCampaignMember.MailNumber__c}, 1) - 1) * 20 + 1, 20))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>fReleased</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>AND(NOT(ISBLANK({!rCampaignMember.MailBatchReleasedOn__c})), {!rCampaignMember.MailBatchReleasedOn__c} &lt;= {!$Flow.CurrentDate})</expression>
    </formulas>
